 "notes_for_editor": "Moderate evidence. Primary: the NRHP nomination, four Light-House Board reports (1896, 1899, 1900, 1901) and the 1917 Bulletin; the 1902, 1908-12 and 1917 events rest on LighthouseFriends and New England Lighthouses (both modern, copyrighted; facts only, one short 1910 quotation of the keeper that both repeat). Chronicling America searches (Loughborough with Greens Ledge, Green's Ledge, Greens Reef, 1910 and 1917) returned no pages, so newspaper accounts of the 1910 and 1912 episodes were not read; LighthouseFriends cites the Harrisburg Telegraph of 12 Mar 1910 and the Portsmouth Daily Herald of 27 Feb 1911. The Lighthouse Board reports for 1902 and later and the Commissioner reports are not in the corpus (Commissioner 1915-22 volume has a riprap estimate of $9,900 for Greens Ledge, year not determined, not used). Conflicts left in the text: lens date (NRHP Feb 1901 vs 1902), De Luce's end year (1904 vs 1908), 1910 departure date (1 vs 2 March) and paycheck ($49.69 vs $44.69), food during the abandonment, auction price ($130,000 vs $150,000), Radio City riprap year (the Society says 1932 and 1933), and the January 1901 vs May 1901 dates for the foundation. Light-House Board report page numbers are scan pages, not printed pages. The Society's WWII, hurricane-wave and Gatsby claims are unverified and mostly left out. Kiarskou name: USLHS Kiarskou, others Kiarskon. USLHS lists Oscar L. Garfield '(at least 1969-1960)' which is impossible; kept without dates. Current characteristic differs between sources (Al Fl W 20s in our record; Wikipedia gives other values), not stated in the story. Roster is from USLHS; 'Andrew J. Simso, Jr.' in the archive is 'II' in New England Lighthouses.",
